+        "id": "uxCDg0ioWh70"
+      },
+      "source": [
+        "# Constant Pressure Simulation"
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "cell_type": "markdown",
+      "metadata": {
+        "id": "dFK0Dew5MwXt"
+      },
+      "source": [
+        "Here we demonstrate some code to run a simulation at in the NPT ensemble with constant temperature and pressure. We start off by setting up some parameters of the simulation. This will include a pressure schedule that will start off at a relatively low pressure before instantaneously trippling the pressure. \n",
+        "\n",
+        "Note that unlike in the case of NVT and NVE simulations, NPT simulations must be performed with `periodic_general` boundary conditions. For now NPT simulations must be performed with fractional coordinates, where the atom positions are stored in the unit cube. This restriction can likely be relaxed in the future, if it were desirable."
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "cell_type": "code",
+      "metadata": {
+        "id": "yGdrjCj1Wm9J"
+      },
+      "source": [
+        "N = 400\n",
+        "dimension = 2\n",
+        "box = quantity.box_size_at_number_density(N, 0.8, 2)\n",
+        "dt = 5e-3\n",
+        "displacement, shift = space.periodic_general(box) \n",
+        "\n",
+        "kT = np.float32(0.01)\n",
+        "P = lambda t: np.where(t < 100.0, 0.05, 0.15)"
+      ],
+      "execution_count": null,
+      "outputs": []
+    },
+    {
+      "cell_type": "markdown",
+      "metadata": {
+        "id": "uFrxHj12M3X1"
+      },
+      "source": [
+        "Next we need to generate some random positions as well as particle sizes. Because we are using `periodic_general` boundary conditions with fractional coordinates, we produce initial particle positions in the unit cube."
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "cell_type": "code",
+      "metadata": {
+        "id": "rEic-SLigNIa"
+      },
+      "source": [
+        "key = random.PRNGKey(0)"
+      ],
+      "execution_count": null,
+      "outputs": []
+    },
+    {
+      "cell_type": "code",
+      "metadata": {
+        "id": "5ApXCCgdWm9O"
+      },
+      "source": [
+        "key, split = random.split(key)\n",
+        "R = random.uniform(split, (N, dimension), dtype=np.float64)\n",
+        "\n",
+        "# The system ought to be a 50:50 mixture of two types of particles, one\n",
+        "# large and one small.\n",
+        "sigma = np.array([[1.0, 1.2], [1.2, 1.4]])\n",
+        "N_2 = int(N / 2)\n",
+        "species = np.where(np.arange(N) < N_2, 0, 1)"
+      ],
+      "execution_count": null,
+      "outputs": []
+    },
+    {
+      "cell_type": "markdown",
+      "metadata": {
+        "id": "hjPUEPcwM6jc"
+      },
+      "source": [
+        "Then we need to construct our simulation operators."
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "cell_type": "code",
+      "metadata": {
+        "id": "B1xXV_FmWm9Q"
+      },
+      "source": [
+        "energy_fn = energy.soft_sphere_pair(displacement, species=species, sigma=sigma)\n",
+        "\n",
+        "init, apply = simulate.npt_nose_hoover(energy_fn, shift, dt, P(0.), kT)\n",
+        "state = init(key, R, box)"
+      ],
+      "execution_count": null,
+      "outputs": []
+    },
+    {
+      "cell_type": "markdown",
+      "metadata": {
+        "id": "hJRvIrfiNAgV"
+      },
+      "source": [
+        "Now let's actually do the simulation. To do this we'll write a small function that performs a single step of the simulation. This function will keep track of the temperature, the extended Hamiltonian of the Nose-Hoover dynamics, and the current particle positions."
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "cell_type": "code",
+      "metadata": {
+        "id": "1rtYEp_LP35v"
+      },
+      "source": [
+        "write_every = 100\n",
+        "\n",
+        "def step_fn(i, state_and_log):\n",
+        "  state, log = state_and_log\n",
+        "\n",
+        "  t = i * dt\n",
+        "\n",
+        "  # Log information about the simulation.\n",
+        "  T = quantity.temperature(state.velocity)\n",
+        "  log['kT'] = ops.index_update(log['kT'], i, T)\n",
+        "\n",
+        "  box = simulate.npt_box(state)\n",
+        "  KE = quantity.kinetic_energy(state.velocity)\n",
+        "  P_measured = quantity.pressure(energy_fn, state.position, box, KE)\n",
+        "  log['P'] = ops.index_update(log['P'], i, P_measured)\n",
+        "\n",
+        "  H = simulate.npt_nose_hoover_invariant(energy_fn, state, P(t), kT)\n",
+        "  log['H'] = ops.index_update(log['H'], i, H)\n",
+        "  \n",
+        "  # Record positions every `write_every` steps.\n",
+        "  pos = space.transform(box, state.position)\n",
+        "  log['position'] = lax.cond(i % write_every == 0,\n",
+        "                             lambda p: ops.index_update(p, \n",
+        "                                                        i // write_every, \n",
+        "                                                        pos),\n",
+        "                             lambda p: p,\n",
+        "                             log['position'])\n",
+        "\n",
+        "  # Take a simulation step.\n",
+        "  state = apply(state, pressure=P(t))\n",
+        "  \n",
+        "  return state, log"
+      ],
+      "execution_count": null,
+      "outputs": []
+    },
